OL,3,GNEWSABlind 101-year-old veteran to
OL,4,Amarch at Cenotaph
OL,5,
OL,6,FA blind 101-year-old World War Two
OL,7,Fveteran is preparing to march at the
OL,8,FCenotaph for the first time on
OL,9,FRemembrance Sunday.
OL,11,FGwynneth Pedler, from Dulwich,
OL,12,Fsouth-east London, will join more than
OL,13,F40 other blind veterans in honour of
OL,14,Ftheir fallen comrades.
OL,16,FPedler joined the Women's Royal Naval
OL,17,FService (WRNS) in 1944 and was posted
OL,18,Fto Crail, near St Andrews, where she
OL,19,Fworked as an air mechanic. She cleaned
OL,20,Fand maintained the guns used by airmen
OL,21,Fwho were learning to drop torpedoes.
OL,23,APub: 08-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
